  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "Number of metal ions characterized by flame test among the following is _________.<br/><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The flame test is used to visually determine the identity of an unknown metal or metalloid ion based on the characteristic colour the salt turns the flame of a Bunsen burner. The heat of the flame excites the electrons of the metal ions, causing them to emit visible light.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>Crimson</mi><mo> </mo><mi>red</mi><mo> </mo><mi>colour</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>Blue</mi><mo> </mo><mi>green</mi><mo> </mo><mi>colour</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msup><mi>Ca</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>Brick</mi><mo> </mo><mi>red</mi><mo> </mo><mi>colour</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><msup><mi>Ba</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mo> </mo><mi>Pale</mi><mo> </mo><mi>green</mi><mo> </mo><mi>colour</mi></math></p><p>Hence, the answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
